<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia names Samuel as competition council head.</title>
<headline>Australia names Samuel as competition council head.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Australian government on Tuesday named businessman and lawyer Graeme Samuel as new chief of the National Competition Council, replacing Tony Daniels.</p>
<p>Samuel, 50, a company director and corporate consultant, has a background in commerce and law and has been a member of the council since it was formed in 1995, Treasurer Peter Costello said in a statement.</p>
<p>Samuel will quit as president of the Australian Chamber of Commerce and Industry to take up the presidency of the Melbourne-based competition agency.</p>
